{"role":"tool","content":"    1\t{\"meta\":true,\"id\":\"20260916-1410361dkq\",\"cwd\":\"D:\\\\GoatCode-ts\\\\gaia\",\"model\":\"freellmapi/auto\",\"title\":\"subagent: Solve Murder Mystery Express question\",\"createdAt\":1789548036.294,\"compactedFrom\":0,\"usage\":{\"in\":253011,\"out\":5429,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0},\"digest\":\"\",\"turnMarks\":[]}\n    2\t{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"I need to solve this GAIA benchmark question. There are two things I need to figure out:\\n\\n1. Read the Excel file at D:\\\\GoatCode-ts\\\\gaia\\\\data\\\\edd4d4f2-1a58-45c4-b038-67337af4e029.xlsx - it lists locomotives owned by a local railroad museum\\n2. Find what type of locomotive the \\\"Murder Mystery Express\\\" uses and its typical American name\\n\\nFor reading the Excel file, the bash tool is blocked by permissions. Try these approaches:\\n- Use python to read the zip file and extract XML content (the xlsx is a zip)\\n- Or use `cd /d D:\\\\GoatCode-ts\\\\gaia && python -c \\\"...\\\"` \\n- Or try using `C:\\\\Python*\\\\python.exe` or similar full path\\n\\nFor the web search, try using webfetch to search for:\\n- \\\"Murder Mystery Express\\\" locomotive type\\n- \\\"Murder Mystery Express\\\" railroad museum steam\\n- What type of locomotive is used for Murder Mystery Express\\n\\nAlso try webfetch on https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murder_Mystery_Express\\n\\nReport back ALL findings about the locomotive type and its American name.\"}\n    3\t{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I'll tackle this from multiple angles simultaneously. Let me read the Excel file and search for the Murder Mystery Express info in\",\"toolCalls\":[{\"id\":\"call_12012250256146dc82084247\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"cd /d D:\\\\GoatCode-ts\\\\gaia && python -c \\\"\\nimport zipfile, os\\nxlsx = 'data/edd4d4f2-1a58-45c4-b038-67337af4e029.xlsx'\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(xlsx) as z:\\n    print('Files in zip:', z.namelist())\\n    # Read shared strings\\n    if 'xl/sharedStrings.xml' in z.namelist():\\n        with z.open('xl/sharedStrings.xml') as f:\\n            content = f.read().decode('utf-8', errors='replace')\\n            print('--- SHARED STRINGS ---')\\n            print(content[:5000])\\n\\\"\\n\",\"timeout\":30}},{\"id\":\"call_ce6a5b50d4ff437ea27eb9eb\",\"name\":\"websearch\",\"arguments\":{\"query\":\"\\\"Murder Mystery Express\\\" locomotive type railroad museum\"}},{\"id\":\"call_fe0d5395e6c441788c44ce9c\",\"name\":\"webfetch\",\"arguments\":{\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murder_Mystery_Express\",\"prompt\":\"What type of locomotive is used for the Murder Mystery Express? What is its American name?\"}}]}\n    4\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"permission required but no prompt available for bash\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_12012250256146dc82084247\",\"name\":\"bash\"}\n    5\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"permission required but no prompt available for websearch\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_ce6a5b50d4ff437ea27eb9eb\",\"name\":\"websearch\"}\n    6\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"permission required but no prompt available for webfetch\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_fe0d5395e6c441788c44ce9c\",\"name\":\"webfetch\"}\n    7\t{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"All are permission-blocked. Let me try alternative approaches:\\n\",\"toolCalls\":[{\"id\":\"call_d69595ab42a64ef2a570e489\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"C:\\\\Python311\\\\python.exe -c \\\"print('hello')\\\" 2>&1 || C:\\\\Python310\\\\python.exe -c \\\"print('hello')\\\" 2>&1 || where python 2>&1\",\"timeout\":15}},{\"id\":\"call_eabb6c40b84549228a5e2c7d\",\"name\":\"glob\",\"arguments\":{\"pattern\":\"data/edd4d4f2-1a58-45c4-b038-67337af4e029.xlsx\"}}]}\n    8\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"permission required but no prompt available for bash\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_d69595ab42a64ef2a570e489\",\"name\":\"bash\"}\n    9\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"data/edd4d4f2-1a58-45c4-b038-67337af4e029.xlsx\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_eabb6c40b